### Architecture Notes
- Verified src/owlbear/daemon.py already satisfies the recommended call-site offload pattern from docs/research/error-journal-async.md: _log_to_journal() is async and uses wait asyncio.to_thread(journal.log, ...).
- Verified _recover_from_error() awaits _log_to_journal() at each daemon call site, which contains the async boundary in the assembly layer where daemon.py belongs.
- Verified src/owlbear/core/context_hook.py, src/owlbear/voice/tts.py, and src/owlbear/tools/web_search.py already use syncio.to_thread, so the implementation matches established codebase precedent.
- Verified 	ests/test_daemon_journal_async.py and 	ests/test_daemon_async_contract.py both pass today (26 passed), so the tracker can point at live executable evidence rather than only archived notes.
- Verified ErrorJournal and JsonlStore remain synchronous, keeping the async adaptation at the daemon call site and avoiding unnecessary API expansion or layer violations.
- Moving #541 to 	odo would create a duplicate builder handoff for scope that already landed. The correct action is to keep it in acklog as a historical tracker with explicit superseding AC.

